  const adviceLocales={
    en:{riven:['Secure one battlefield first, then turn ready-entry units and Blade of the Exile into a repeatable tempo loop.','Favored into slower setup and gear engines once a battlefield is controlled.','Wide early pressure and removal before the first conquest can break the engine.','Keep a low-cost opener, protect the first hold, and do not commit every resource to one combat.'],kennen:['Play cards from outside the hand to empower Kennen while Captain and Hidden cards keep the engine supplied.','Strong in long midrange games where repeated value matters.','Fast disruption can force interaction before the engine becomes self-sustaining.','Lead with expendable units, test reactions, then deploy Kennen with protection available.'],kaisa:['Combine Fury damage with Mind selection, preserving enough Power to attack without losing access to Reactions.','Punishes unit-dense decks that lack instant protection.','Large single threats trade poorly into bounce, counters and durable defense.','Score with replaceable units first; commit Kai’Sa only when she creates immediate value.'],rengar:['Use dense units and combat boosts so every movement creates a favorable battlefield exchange.','Excellent against decks defending with only a few key units.','Struggles when opponents score across multiple fields or bypass combat.','Choose the battlefield that supports repeated attacks and save one burst turn for the final points.'],akali:['Convert low-cost mobility and protection into early battlefield control, then chain movement for points.','Punishes expensive curves and slow interaction windows.','Wide boards and cheap unconditional removal stretch protection too far.','Mulligan for an actual first-two-turn curve and deploy the core only for immediate value.'],vex:['Slow the opponent with Hidden cards and Reactions, then let high-value units take over the board.','Strong against one large telegraphed attack.','Can run out of answers against pressure on several battlefields.','Save premium reactions for the real scoring turn, not the first small unit.'],irelia:['Treat gear, ready effects and movement as one combo rather than isolated value cards.','Can outmaneuver opponents with fixed combat timing.','Cheap counters, gear removal and repeated small-unit removal break the chain.','Start the full sequence only after confirming the opponent cannot interrupt the key equip.'],azir:['Build a durable Gear engine and plan rune use several turns ahead.','Excels when opponents cannot remove gear and must win through combat.','Early burst and multi-field scoring can race the setup.','Secure one inexpensive hold first; when behind, stop adding value pieces and contest points immediately.']},
    ja:{riven:['まず戦場を1つ確保し、準備状態で出るユニットとBlade of the Exileでテンポを継続します。','遅いセットアップやGear中心の相手に有利。','最初の征服前の横展開と除去が弱点。','低コストの初動を残し、最初のHoldを守り、1戦闘に全資源を使わない。'],kennen:['手札外からカードをプレイしてKennenを強化し、CaptainとHiddenでリソースを継続。','長いミッドレンジ戦で反復価値が強い。','エンジン完成前の高速妨害が弱点。','小型で反応を確認し、保護を残してKennenを展開。'],kaisa:['Furyの打点とMindの選択力を合わせ、Reaction用Powerを残す。','即時保護が少ないユニット中心の相手に強い。','バウンス、カウンター、堅い防御が苦手。','交換可能なユニットで先に得点し、Kai’Saは即時価値が出る場面で投入。'],rengar:['高密度ユニットと戦闘強化で、移動を有利交換に変える。','少数の中核ユニットで守る相手に強い。','多戦場への圧力や戦闘を避ける得点が苦手。','継続攻撃しやすい戦場を選び、最後の得点用に爆発ターンを残す。'],akali:['低コストの機動力と保護で先に戦場を取り、連続移動で得点。','重いカーブと遅い干渉に強い。','横展開と安い除去が弱点。','最初の2ターンの動きを優先し、中核は即時価値がある時だけ出す。'],vex:['HiddenとReactionで遅らせ、高価値ユニットで盤面を取る。','予告された一度の大攻撃に強い。','複数戦場への同時圧力が苦手。','重要なReactionは本当の得点ターンまで温存。'],irelia:['Gear、Ready、移動を一つのコンボとして扱う。','戦闘タイミングが固定された相手を動きで上回れる。','安い無効化、Gear除去、小型除去が弱点。','相手が主要Equipを止められないと確認してから連鎖開始。'],azir:['Gearエンジンを構築し、数ターン先のルーン配分を計画。','Gear処理がなく正面戦闘する相手に強い。','高速展開と多戦場得点が苦手。','安く1つのHoldを確保し、劣勢時は価値より即時の得点争いを優先。']}
  };
